328:
This chapter seeks to encourage the development of desirable land use patterns within the city in accordance with the city's comprehensive plan. The promotion of sound land use patterns is intended to reduce or eliminate the occurrence of certain conditions that can threaten the general health, safety and welfare of the residents of the city. This chapter serves the following purposes:
(1) Promote adequate living conditions and sustained suitability of neighborhoods;
(2) Protect property against blight and depreciation;
(3) Promote the proper location, height, bulk, size of buildings and other structures, the size of the yards, courts and the use of other open spaces, the use of buildings, structures and land for trade, industry, residence, recreation, agriculture, forestry, conservation, sanitation, protection against floods, public activities and other purposes; and
(4) Encourage the most appropriate use of land, buildings and structures; and for other purposes.
(Ord. of 6-3-1997, § 1-4; Res. of 11-3-2020, att.(1-4))

346:
